    {
      "evidence_id": "e-d591aed9ada84e7951df",
      "text": "The most species-rich families in the flora of Kimolos are the Fabaceae (73 taxa), \nfollowed by the Asteraceae (53 taxa) and Poaceae (47 taxa). These three families \naccount for more than one third of the total flora (39.77%). Caryophyllaceae \n(29 taxa), Brassicaceae (23 taxa), Orchidaceae (18 taxa) and Apiaceae (12 taxa) are \nalso well represented.",
